    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-100100000003',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Augusta Ada King, Countess of Lovelace (née Byron; 10 December 1815 – 27 November 1852), also known as Ada Lovelace, was an English mathematician and writer chiefly known for work on Charles Babbage''s proposed mechanical general-purpose computer, the analytical engine. She was the first to recognise the machine had applications beyond pure calculation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lovelace is often considered the first computer programmer. Lovelace was the only legitimate child of poet Lord Byron and reformer Anne Isabella Milbanke. Lord Byron separated from his wife a month after Ada was born, and died when she was eight. Although often ill in childhood, Lovelace pursued her studies assiduously. She married William King in 1835."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Lord"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Lovelace"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Ada"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Ada Lovelace","pageid":974,"revision_id":1360639004,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ada_Lovelace","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
    true,
    'approved',
    NOW()
  ),
  (
    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-100100000004',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adelaide ( AD-il-ayd; Kaurna: Tarndanya [ˈd̪̥aɳɖaɲa]) is the capital and most populous city of South Australia, as well as the fifth-most populous city in Australia. The name \"Adelaide\" may refer to either Greater Adelaide (including the Adelaide Hills) or the Adelaide city centre; the demonym Adelaidean is used to denote the city and the residents of Adelaide."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The traditional owners of the Adelaide region are the Kaurna, with the name Tarndanya referring to the area of the city centre and surrounding Park Lands, in the Kaurna language. Adelaide is situated on the Adelaide Plains north of the Fleurieu Peninsula, between the Gulf St Vincent in the west and the Mount Lofty Ranges in the east."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Mount"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Ranges"}],"difficulty":"easy","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Adelaide","pageid":1148,"revision_id":1363592535,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelaide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
