  (
    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-100100000024',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The World Health Organization (WHO) is a specialized agency of the United Nations (UN) which coordinates responses to international public health issues and emergencies. It is headquartered in Geneva, Switzerland, and has six regional offices and 150 field offices worldwide."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Only sovereign states are eligible to join, and it is the largest intergovernmental health organization at the international level. The WHO''s stated purpose is to achieve the highest possible level of health for all the world''s people, defining health as \"a state of complete physical, mental and social well-being and not merely the absence of disease or infirmity.\""}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"150"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Organization"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Health"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"World Health Organization","pageid":33583,"revision_id":1361523187,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Health_Organization","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
    true,
    'approved',
    NOW()
  ),
  (
    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-100100000025',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Amazon rainforest, also called the Amazon jungle, Amazonia, or simply the Amazon, is a moist broadleaf tropical rainforest in the Amazon biome that covers most of the Amazon basin of South America. This basin encompasses 7 million km2 (2. 7 million sq mi), of which 6 million km2 (2. 3 million sq mi) are covered by the rainforest."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This region includes territory belonging to nine nations and 3,344 indigenous territories. The majority of the forest, 60%, is in Brazil, followed by Peru with 13%, Colombia with 10%, and with minor amounts in Bolivia, Ecuador, French Guiana, Guyana, Suriname, and Venezuela."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"7"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Guyana"},{"id":"kw3","text":"basin"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Amazon rainforest","pageid":48139,"revision_id":1362682846,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_rainforest","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
    true,
    'approved',
    NOW()
  ),
  (
    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-100100000026',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Mona Lisa is a half-length portrait painting by the Italian artist Leonardo da Vinci. Considered an archetypal masterpiece of the Italian Renaissance, it has been described as \"the best known, the most visited, the most written about, the most sung about, [and] the most parodied work of art in the world.\""}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The painting''s novel qualities include the subject''s enigmatic expression, the monumentality of the composition, the subtle modelling of forms, and the atmospheric illusionism. The painting has been traditionally considered to depict the Italian noblewoman Lisa del Giocondo. It is painted in oil on a white poplar panel. Leonardo never gave the painting to the Giocondo family."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Giocondo"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Italian"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Leonardo"},{"id":"kw4","text":"Lisa"},{"id":"kw5","text":"Renaissance"}],"difficulty":"hard","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Mona Lisa","pageid":70889,"revision_id":1363473826,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mona_Lisa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
    true,
    'approved',
    NOW()
  ),
  (
    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-100100000027',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Sahara (, ) is a desert spanning North Africa. With an area of 9,200,000 square kilometres (3,600,000 sq mi), it is the largest hot desert in the world and the third-largest desert overall, smaller only than the deserts of Antarctica and the northern Arctic."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The name \"Sahara\" is derived from Arabic: صَحَارَى, romanized: ṣaḥārā /sˤaħaːraː/, a broken plural form of ṣaḥrā'' (صَحْرَاء /sˤaħraːʔ/), meaning \"desert\". The desert covers much of North Africa, excluding the fertile region on the Mediterranean Sea coast, the Atlas Mountains of the Maghreb, and the Nile Valley in Egypt and the Sudan."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Africa"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Arabic"}],"difficulty":"easy","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Sahara","pageid":325363,"revision_id":1362700122,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sahara","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
    true,
    'approved',
    NOW()
  ),
  (
    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-100100000028',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Antarctica  is Earth''s southernmost and least-populated continent. Situated almost entirely south of the Antarctic Circle and surrounded by the Southern Ocean (also known as the Antarctic Ocean), it contains the geographic South Pole. Antarctica is the fifth-largest continent, being about 40% larger than Europe, and has an area of 14,200,000 km2 (5,500,000 sq mi)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Most of Antarctica is covered by the Antarctic ice sheet, with an average thickness of 1. 9 km (1. 2 mi). Antarctica is, on average, the coldest, driest, and windiest of the continents, and has the highest average elevation. It is mainly a polar desert, with annual precipitation of over 200 mm (8 in) along the coast and far less inland."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"1"},{"id":"kw2","text":"5,500,000"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Antarctica"},{"id":"kw4","text":"200"},{"id":"kw5","text":"14,200,000"}],"difficulty":"hard","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Antarctica","pageid":18959138,"revision_id":1363609435,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antarctica","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
