    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The PTS Lactose-N,N’-Diacetylchitobiose (Lac) Family (TC# 4.A.3) includes several sequenced lactose porters of Gram-positive bacteria, as well as the Escherichia coli and Borrelia burgdorferi N,N''-diacetylchitobiose (Chb) porters. It is part of the PTS-GFL superfamily. The former can transport aromatic β-glucosides and cellobiose, as well as Chb. However, only Chb induces expression of the chb operon."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Chb"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Borrelia"}],"difficulty":"easy","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"PTS Lactose-N,N''-Diacetylchitobiose Family","pageid":51467419,"revision_id":1282368127,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PTS_Lactose-N,N%27-Diacetylchitobiose_Family","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
