    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Kingsley Clarence Dassanaike ( də-sə-NY-ə-kə Sinhala: කිංස්ලි ක්ලැරන්ස් දසනායක; Tamil: தசநாயக்க கிளாரென்ஸ் கிங்ஸ்லி; born 19 June 1914, date of death unknown), the first non-foreign Principal of the Ceylon School for the Deaf & Blind in Ratmalana, Sri Lanka was the inventor of the Sinhala Braille system, and served as the Chairman of the Extension Scout Committee for disabled Scouts of the World Organization of the Scout Movement as well as National Headquarters Commissioner, District Commissioner for Colombo of the Sri Lanka Scout Association from 1958 to 1963 and acting District Commissioner of Moratuwa–Piliyandala in the 1960s."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"District"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Organization"}],"difficulty":"easy","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Kingsley C. Dassanaike","pageid":52471687,"revision_id":1354936085,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingsley_C._Dassanaike","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
