    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Leicaflex series of high-end single-lens reflex 35 mm format film cameras were introduced by Leitz Camera in 1964. The first camera body was paired with the new R bayonet series of lenses. Three model of the cameras were sold by Leitz; the Leicaflex Standard, the Leicaflex SL and the Leicaflex SL2."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Late into the market with high prices and limited range of lenses and accessories, Leicaflex sales were below expectations and production ended in 1976. However, the production of the R mount lenses continued and were paired with the new Leica R3 that was developed in cooperation with Minolta, together with the Minolta XE bodies."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"lenses"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Minolta"},{"id":"kw3","text":"1976"},{"id":"kw4","text":"Camera"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Leicaflex","pageid":67434915,"revision_id":1345481612,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leicaflex","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
