    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iran–Turkmenistan relations are the foreign relations between Iran and Turkmenistan. The two countries share a 1,148 km-long border and have long-standing historical ties. Following Turkmenistan’s independence from the Soviet Union in 1991, the two countries have maintained friendly relations and established diplomatic relations in 1992. Since then, they have developed cooperation in various fields, including economics, transport, infrastructure development, and energy."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"1992"},{"id":"kw2","text":"relations"},{"id":"kw3","text":"1991"},{"id":"kw4","text":"Turkmenistan"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Iran–Turkmenistan relations","pageid":11740063,"revision_id":1360111025,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran%E2%80%93Turkmenistan_relations","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
