    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Eddie Conde Gil (born February 7, 1944, in Masbate) is a Filipino singer and comedian who attempted to run for President of the Philippines during the 2004 presidential elections. However, he was disqualified from running by the Commission on Elections, citing his inability to begin a national campaign and marking him as a ''nuisance candidate.''"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Gil appealed his disqualification to the Philippine Supreme Court, where it was upheld. A self-proclaimed billionaire, he promised fellow Filipinos to pay off the national debt with his own finances. But in an embarrassing occurrence in one of his ''campaign sorties'' in Mindanao, particularly Cagayan de Oro, Gil wasn''t even able to afford the hotel accommodations."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Filipinos"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Supreme"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Gil"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Eddie Gil","pageid":25974299,"revision_id":1348241928,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eddie_Gil","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
