    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Jan Andrzej Zakrzewski (24 February 1920, in Skierniewice – 22 April 2007, in Warsaw) was a Polish journalist, writer, translator. Member of the Stowarzyszenie Dziennikarzy Polskich, Stowarzyszenie Pisarzy Polskich, International PEN. Awarded the Knight''s Cross of the Polonia Restituta (1975), Cross of Merit (1973) and Cross of Valour."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Zakrzewski was a soldier of Invasion of Poland (1939) and he also fought in Norway (1940). During the World War II he was an officer of Polish Armed Forces in the West. After back to Poland Zakrzewski led the art agency \"Artos\" in Wrocław (1950)."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Cross"},{"id":"kw2","text":"West"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Wrocław"},{"id":"kw4","text":"24 February 1920"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Jan Andrzej Zakrzewski","pageid":13184710,"revision_id":1354051953,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jan_Andrzej_Zakrzewski","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
