    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ethiopia has been a member of the United Nations since November 13, 1945. The membership stipulated to prevent from external attacks and invasions and to maintain envisaged \"collective security\" despite the being ineffective and the League shortcomings following Italian invasion of the country in 1935."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Since 1950s, Ethiopia dispatched its first peacekeeping forces to Korea and Congo and evolved in personnels after 1990s missions some African states. Currently, Ethiopia has 80,000 peacekeeping active forces. The UN largely covers development and humanitarian plan in Ethiopia."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Italian"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Congo"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Ethiopia"},{"id":"kw4","text":"peacekeeping"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Ethiopia and the United Nations","pageid":71630183,"revision_id":1317967242,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethiopia_and_the_United_Nations","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
