    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-1001000001bf',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Semaan (Syriac: ܫܡܥܘܢ, romanized: Šemʿōn Arabic: سمعان, romanized: Semʻān), also spelled Sem''an, Semán, Simaan, Sim''an, Samaan, Sam''an, or Sima''an, is a masculine given name mainly found in the Levant of West Asia. It can also be used as a surname."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The name is derived from the Semitic root word/verb sema or shema, which means “to hear”; thus, the meaning of Semaan becomes “the one who hears or listens” in both Syriac and Arabic. The name''s equivalent in Hebrew is Shimon or Shim''on (שִׁמְעוֹן‎), which also has the same meaning. The Hebrew form is also the origin for the Arabic name."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Hebrew"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Shim''on"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Shimon"},{"id":"kw4","text":"Syriac"},{"id":"kw5","text":"Sim''an"}],"difficulty":"hard","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Semaan","pageid":27479593,"revision_id":1361898267,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semaan","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
