    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-1001000001c9',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Till Death Us Do Part is a British television sitcom that aired on BBC1 from 1965 to 1975. The show was first broadcast in 1965 as a Comedy Playhouse pilot, then as seven series between 1966 and 1975. In 1981, ITV continued the sitcom for six episodes, calling it Till Death.... The BBC produced a sequel from 1985 until 1992, In Sickness and in Health."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created by Johnny Speight, Till Death Us Do Part centred on the East End Garnett family, led by patriarch Alf Garnett (Warren Mitchell), a reactionary white working-class man who holds racist and anti-socialist views. His long-suffering wife Else was played by Dandy Nichols, and his daughter Rita by Una Stubbs."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Nichols"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Garnett"},{"id":"kw3","text":"BBC"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Till Death Us Do Part","pageid":36986,"revision_id":1353141679,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Till_Death_Us_Do_Part","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
