    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hitler''s Letters and Notes is a book by Werner Maser. It is a collection of Adolf Hitler’s personal correspondence and private notations with comments by Maser. It reproduces photo-facsimiles of the handwritten original documents, with translations thereof, from the age of 17 until his death."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Maser contends that the book casts new light onto the development of Hitler''s political philosophy. It was first published in German as Hitlers Briefe und Notizen: sein Weltbild in handschriftlichen Dokumenten in 1973. Heinemann (London) published a slightly adapted translation (by Arnold Pomerans) as a 390-page hardcover in 1974, followed by Harper & Row in the United States."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Pomerans"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Briefe"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Notes"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Hitler''s Letters and Notes","pageid":2677844,"revision_id":1335418748,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hitler%27s_Letters_and_Notes","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
