    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nobuaki Kaneko (金子 ノブアキ, 金子 信昭, Kaneko Nobuaki; born 5 June 1981) is a Japanese drummer and actor. He is nicknamed Akkun (あっくん) and N. K. He is a member of the rock band Rize. He is represented with Itoh Company and his label is Illchill. He graduated from Horikoshi High School. Kaneko''s father was Johnny Yoshinaga who was also a drummer, and his mother is singer Mari Kaneko."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"His younger brother is Kensuke Kaneko (known as KenKen) who is the bassist of Rize, and the brothers formed a rhythm section. In November 2013, Kaneko married a non-celebrity woman who is a former model."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Kaneko"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Itoh"}],"difficulty":"easy","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Nobuaki Kaneko","pageid":53452153,"revision_id":1351766353,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nobuaki_Kaneko","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
