    'd1000001-0000-4000-8000-100100000252',
    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mare reproductive loss syndrome (MRLS) is a syndrome consisting of equine abortions and three related nonreproductive syndromes which occur in horses of all breeds, sexes, and ages. MRLS was first observed in the U. S. state of Kentucky in a three-week period around May 5, 2001, when about 20–30% of Kentucky''s pregnant mares suffered abortions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A primary infectious cause was rapidly ruled out, and the search began for a candidate toxin. No abortifacient toxins were identified. In the spring of 2001, Kentucky had experienced an extraordinarily heavy infestation of eastern tent caterpillars (ETCs). An epidemiological study showed ETCs to be associated with MRLS."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"May"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Kentucky"},{"id":"kw3","text":"2001"},{"id":"kw4","text":"syndrome"},{"id":"kw5","text":"ETCs"}],"difficulty":"hard","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Mare reproductive loss syndrome","pageid":4016448,"revision_id":1306056893,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mare_reproductive_loss_syndrome","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
