    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Vrijdagmarkt (Dutch pronunciation: [ˈvrɛidɑxmɑr(ə)kt]; \"Friday Market\") is a city square in the historic centre of Ghent, East Flanders, Belgium. It is named after the weekly tradition to stage a market every Friday morning. As one of the oldest squares in Ghent, it played an important role in the city''s history."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Friday"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Ghent"},{"id":"kw3","text":"Vrijdagmarkt"},{"id":"kw4","text":"East"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Vrijdagmarkt, Ghent","pageid":51868770,"revision_id":1341461876,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vrijdagmarkt,_Ghent","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
