    'a1000001-0000-4000-8000-000000000001',
    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Kalamazoo Baptists football program, 1910–1919 (also referred to as the Kalamazoo Orange and Black, later known as the Kalamazoo Hornets) represented Kalamazoo College in American football during the school''s third decade of college football. The team competed as a member of the Michigan Intercollegiate Athletic Association (MIAA). Highlights of the decade include the following:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The 1916 Kalamazoo Baptists football team enjoyed a perfect season with a 7–0 record and won the MIAA championship. The team also set a school scoring record with a 108–0 victory over Grand Rapids Veterinary. The 1919 Kalamazoo Baptists football team compiled a 5–2 record (4–0 in conference games) and won the MIAA championship."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Baptists"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Athletic"},{"id":"kw3","text":"championship"}],"difficulty":"medium","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Kalamazoo Baptists football, 1910–1919","pageid":79537260,"revision_id":1341926763,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalamazoo_Baptists_football,_1910%E2%80%931919","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
