    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A sprayer is a device used to spray a liquid, where sprayers are commonly used for projection of water, weed killers, crop performance materials, pest maintenance chemicals, as well as manufacturing and production line ingredients. In agriculture, a sprayer is a piece of equipment that is used to apply herbicides, pesticides, and fertilizers on agricultural crops."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sprayers range in size from man-portable units (typically backpacks with spray guns) to trailed sprayers that are connected to a tractor, to self-propelled units similar to tractors with boom mounts of 4–30 feet (1. 2–9. 1 m) up to 60–151 feet (18–46 m) in length depending on engineering design for tractor and land size."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"9"},{"id":"kw2","text":"tractor"},{"id":"kw3","text":"30"},{"id":"kw4","text":"18"},{"id":"kw5","text":"1"}],"difficulty":"hard","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Sprayer","pageid":8068934,"revision_id":1293546902,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sprayer","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
