    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Walk is a 2015 American biographical drama film directed by Robert Zemeckis, who co-wrote the screenplay with Christopher Browne. It is based on the story of French high-wire artist Philippe Petit''s walk between the Twin Towers of the World Trade Center in 1974."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The film stars Joseph Gordon-Levitt as Petit, alongside Ben Kingsley, Charlotte Le Bon, James Badge Dale, Ben Schwartz, and Steve Valentine. Following its premiere at the New York Film Festival, The Walk was released by Sony Pictures Releasing on September 30, 2015 in the United States in IMAX 3D, and on October 9 in regular 2D and 3D."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Center"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Releasing"}],"difficulty":"easy","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"The Walk (2015 film)","pageid":43021426,"revision_id":1360826130,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Walk_(2015_film)","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
