    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tay was a high official of Ancient Egypt with the main title treasurer. He was in office under Hatshepsut (about 1508–1458 BC) and in the first years of Thutmose III (about 1479 BC to 1425 BC). Tay is only known from a few attestations. He appears in a rock inscription on the island of Sehel, in a letter (P."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Louvre 3230(b)) that is dated by context under Hatshepsut and from a stela found on Sinai. The latter inscription is dated to year 25 under king Thutmose III. Tay is shown here standing behind the king. According to the rock inscription on Sehel he was on a military campaign with the queen to Nubia."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"1425"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Nubia"},{"id":"kw3","text":"dated"},{"id":"kw4","text":"inscription"},{"id":"kw5","text":"25"}],"difficulty":"hard","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Tay (treasurer)","pageid":30481441,"revision_id":1342655953,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tay_(treasurer)","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
