    '{"passage":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Constitutional Court of Georgia (Georgian: საქართველოს საკონსტიტუციო სასამართლო, romanized: sakartvelos sak''onst''it''utsio sasamartlo) is the constitutional court of Georgia, the country''s judicial body of constitutional review, having the greatest significance with the view of securing constitutional provisions and separation of powers, and protecting human rights and freedoms."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Constitutional Court was established in 1996. The legal basis of its organisation and activity is the Constitution of Georgia, the Organic Law of Georgia \"On the Constitutional Court of Georgia\", and the Rules of the Constitutional Court."}]}]},"keywords":[{"id":"kw1","text":"Constitutional"},{"id":"kw2","text":"Rules"}],"difficulty":"easy","source":{"provider":"wikipedia","title":"Constitutional Court of Georgia","pageid":15637876,"revision_id":1363520947,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitutional_Court_of_Georgia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","retrieved_at":"2026-07-11T15:06:19.295Z"}}'::jsonb,
